cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build on this protocol or the fabrication log, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "AoCA: Agents of Chaos Applied. A human-adjudicated cross-model adversarial review protocol with clinical evidence-hierarchy weighting"
version: "2.0.1"
date-released: "2026-09-26"
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Bradley
    given-names: Stephen
    affiliation: "Prosthetic Mind Holdings LLC"
abstract: >-
  AoCA is a procedure for catching errors, misattributed or invented sources,
  overclaiming and sycophancy in AI-drafted documents. It stages structured
  disagreement between model sessions from different families, applies an
  Accuracy Mandate and a clinical evidence hierarchy to the reviewer's own
  findings, and routes every unresolved disagreement to a human decision
  authority. The release includes the protocol versions, prompt templates, a
  single-agent variant, a two-axis citation standard, case studies rebuilt from
  transcripts, and a fabrication log published as a dataset.
keywords:
  - adversarial validation
  - cross-model review
  - hallucination detection
  - citation verification
  - human-in-the-loop
  - evidence hierarchy
